7592186490203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490203 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490203 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490203 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186489563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490203 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f5233b41-f23f-5e4f-b8ad-e6c6136880ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490235 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490235 #edb/ref 1069 "q-147042" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490235 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490235 #edb/ref 1071 "The ratio of T-shirts to pairs of jeans in David's closet is $\\frac{5}{2}.$ If David has $4$ pairs of jeans in his closet, how many T-shirts does David have?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490235 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "34bd5498-60c5-56d4-9f94-63016d557040" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490235 #edb/ref 1074 "The ratio of T-shirts to pairs of jeans in David's closet is $\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of T-shirts and the denominator represents the number of pairs of jeans.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $4$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 2}{2\\times 2}=\\frac{10}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, David has $10$ T-shirts in his closet." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490246 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490246 #edb/ref 1069 "q-147047" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490246 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490246 #edb/ref 1071 "Sophie is baking a pie. The recipe for the pie dough states that the ratio of sugar to melted butter is $\\frac{3}{2}.$ If she decides to use $4$ cups of melted butter, how many cups of sugar does she need to use?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490246 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4cce5310-2253-544b-a45b-5b307f4192ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490246 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that the ratio of sugar to melted butter is $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of cups of sugar and the denominator represents the number of cups of melted butter.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $4$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 2}{2\\times 2}=\\frac{6}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $4$ cups of melted butter, Sophie must use $6$ cups of sugar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490296 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490296 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490296 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490296 #edb/ref 1071 "There are $60$ peaches in Sophia's store. The ratio of peaches to pears is $6:5.$ How many pears are there in Sophia's store?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490296 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bad4ad2c-65e9-50c0-a0af-a1c173627efa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490296 #edb/ref 1074 "We start with the ratio $6:5$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of peaches and the denominator represents the number of pears.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $60$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 10}{5\\times 10}=\\frac{60}{50}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $50$ pears in Sophia's store." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490299 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490299 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60307" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490299 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490299 #edb/ref 1071 "To prepare a homemade nasal spray, the ratio of salt (in grams) to cups of water is $\\frac{5}{2}.$ If Eliza wants to make a nasal spray with $15$ grams of salt, how many cups of water should she use?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490299 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bdac105a-b535-5e32-bc94-795efb94b947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490299 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that the ratio of salt (in grams) to cups of water is $\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the amount of salt and the denominator represents the number of cups of water.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $15$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 3}{2\\times 3}=\\frac{15}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $15$ grams of salt, Eliza must use $6$ cups of water." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
